# Hashed Vite assets must NEVER SPA-fallback to index.html. A stale HTML referencing a retired
# hash (or a Bot Fight interstitial) would otherwise return text/html 200 for /assets/*.js —
# browsers then refuse the module ("Failed to fetch dynamically imported module") and React
# never boots. Status 404 here wins over the catch-all below when no real file matches.
/assets/*  /index.html  404

# Explicit SPA fallback — Cloudflare Pages checks for an exact static-asset match (including the
# prerendered .html files under scripts/prerender.mjs) before evaluating this file, so this only
# ever catches routes with no matching static file: legitimate client-only routes (/dashboard,
# /login, /sign/:token, /status/:token, /admin/analytics, /prepare, etc.) and genuinely unknown
# URLs. functions/_middleware.ts intercepts those before this rewrite when possible: app routes
# get an emptied #root + noindex shell (so crawlers don't see the prerendered homepage), and
# unknown URLs get HTTP 404. This 200 rewrite remains as a safety net if the Function is bypassed.
/*  /index.html  200
